  "created": "2021-07-20T12:01:16.587Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While i certainly miss the 2018 loading screen, i have become used to the new one. However there are some key things that i feel need some serious attention. The first one is the screen that showcases the trust ranking system, with the new ui update and the new nameplates, this screen has become outdated and possibly confusing for anyone who doesnt know about the old nameplates.\nThe second one happens to be the one that has personally annoyed me the  most, and is the one that i feel needs to get taken care of first. The screen discussing the state of NSFW content on vrchat. Ever since this screen has come out, it has been almost unanimously agreed that it means that NSFW content is allowed in private, aslong as you dont stream or share it, however the content is not allowed at all in public or friends/+ worlds. However this is a complete misconception and factually wrong, leading to a massive amount of confusion, and an entire community centered around this content sprouting up and seeping its way into pubic environments and around kids. The ToS, community guidelines, and multiple moderators have come out at different points to state that its not allowed -period-\nI seriously feel this should get taken care of sooner rather than later, because its already caused enough damage.\nMy recommendation would to be either remove the screen entirely, or create a new one that more accurately states what the ruling on this side of content truly is.",
